## 3. Information You Store in Receipt Vault

You may choose to enter information such as:

* product and brand names;
* retailer information;
* purchase dates;
* purchase prices;
* warranty information and expiry dates;
* model and serial numbers;
* notes;
* photographs of receipts; and
* PDF receipt files.

This information is provided by you and is stored locally within the App on your device.

Receipt Vault does not require you to create an account.

## 4. How Your Information Is Used

Information stored in Receipt Vault is used solely to provide the App's functionality, including:

* organising and searching your purchases;
* displaying receipt information;
* calculating and displaying warranty status;
* providing local warranty reminder notifications; and
* creating and restoring backups when you choose to use those features.

Receipt Vault does not use your stored purchase or receipt information for advertising, profiling, or marketing.

## 5. Where Your Information Is Stored

Receipt Vault stores your purchase records, settings and receipt files in the App's private storage on your device.

Receipt Vault does not operate a cloud database or Receipt Vault online account system.

Your information is therefore not routinely transmitted to or stored on Receipt Vault servers.

## 6. Receipt Photos and PDF Files

When you add a receipt photograph or PDF, the selected file is copied into Receipt Vault's private app storage so that it can be retained and displayed by the App.

Receipt files are not automatically uploaded to a remote server.

When you deliberately export or share a backup, the resulting backup file may contain your purchase information and receipt data. Any such transfer is initiated by you and is subject to the security and privacy practices of the destination or sharing service you choose.

## 7. Backup and Restore

Receipt Vault provides a local backup and restore facility.

A backup may contain:

* your purchase information;
* warranty information;
* notes;
* receipt information; and
* the contents of stored receipt files.

Backups are created only when you choose to export them.

You are responsible for keeping exported backup files secure and for deciding where they are stored or shared.

## 8. Notifications

Receipt Vault may request permission to send local notifications for warranty reminders.

These reminders are scheduled on your device and are used to notify you about upcoming or expiring warranties.

Receipt Vault does not use notifications to send advertising or marketing messages.

## 9. Information We Do Not Collect

Receipt Vault does not intentionally collect or transmit:

* your name, unless you choose to include it in information you enter;
* your contacts;
* your precise location;
* your browsing history;
* advertising identifiers for advertising purposes;
* payment card or bank account information;
* account passwords; or
* personal information through a Receipt Vault online account.

Receipt Vault does not contain user accounts or social networking functionality.

## 10. Third-Party Services

Receipt Vault does not operate its own cloud storage or analytics service for your stored receipt and purchase information.

The App may use operating-system and platform components required to provide functions such as file selection, notifications and sharing. When you choose to use those functions, the handling of information by the relevant platform or third-party service is governed by that provider's own privacy policy.

## 11. Data Retention and Deletion

Your information remains stored locally on your device until you delete it, remove the App, or otherwise remove the relevant files.

You can delete individual purchases and associated receipt files using the App's available deletion functions.

You can also remove the App from your device to remove its locally stored application data, subject to the Android operating system's behaviour and any backups you may have created elsewhere.

Exported backup files are separate from the App's local storage. You are responsible for deleting those backup files from any location where you have saved or shared them.

Receipt Vault does not maintain a remote copy of your locally stored information that it can delete on your behalf.

## 12. Security

Receipt Vault is designed to keep your information within the App's private storage on your device.

However, no storage method or electronic device can be guaranteed to be completely secure. You should protect your device with an appropriate screen lock and keep any exported backup files secure.

## 13. Children's Privacy

Receipt Vault is intended for general use and is not specifically directed toward children.

We do not knowingly collect personal information from children through an online service because Receipt Vault does not operate an online account or cloud data collection system.

## 14. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to reflect changes to the App, its functionality, or applicable legal and platform requirements.

The latest version will be made available at the published privacy policy address.

